Subject: gdkarray: Avoid wrapped pointer offsets when shrinking

Base: 34dc3af563f767348ca575827f414a50c0458b0e

added and removed are unsigned sizes. Shrinking wraps their difference
before adding it to end, which UBSan diagnoses as pointer overflow.

Subtract removed before adding added. The intermediate pointer stays
within the old array, and reserve provides space for the final size.
Reuse the existing array tests for ordinary, preallocated, NULL-terminated,
and element-destroying variants.

--- a/gdk/gdkarrayimpl.c
+++ b/gdk/gdkarrayimpl.c
@@ -260,8 +260,8 @@
     }
 
 
-  /* might overflow, but does the right thing */
-  self->end += added - removed;
+  self->end -= removed;
+  self->end += added;
 }
 
 G_GNUC_UNUSED static void
